# Fork preferences (kumaab/ranger)

These are personal preferences for work done in this fork. They sit **on top of**
`ranger-pr-review.mdc` and `ranger-checkstyle.mdc`, which remain authoritative for
everything not listed here.

This file is fork-only and is not part of upstream `apache/ranger`. Exclude it from the
diff of any PR raised against upstream.

## 1. Comment syntax — overrides the codebase norm

Use `/* .. */` block syntax, never `//`. Keep every comment to 2 lines or fewer.

```java
/* single-line form */

/* two-line form, where the explanation continues onto
 * the second and final line. */
```

Applies to comments you add or rewrite. Leave pre-existing comments in untouched code alone.

This diverges from the surrounding code on purpose: `agents-common/src/main/java` carries
roughly 428 `//` line comments against 6 non-javadoc block comments. Nothing enforces either
style — `dev-support/checkstyle.xml` has no comment-style module. The 2-line cap reinforces
the "comments have become too noisy" feedback recorded in `ranger-pr-review.mdc` §5.6; the
syntax is preference. Expect a reviewer nit if the code goes upstream.

## 2. Member order in test classes

`ranger-pr-review.mdc` specifies member order for main sources but not for tests. Apply the
same decreasing-visibility rule, private last:

    @Test methods (public) -> public static nested fixtures -> private helpers

Both shapes exist in the repo today — `TestInlinePolicyEvaluator` puts private helpers before
its nested classes, while `TestRangerAbstractContextEnricher`, `TestJsonUtilsV2` and
`TestRangerResourceEvaluatorsRetriever` put fixtures first. Prefer private-last.

## 3. Reflectively loaded pluggable classes

A class loaded by name from configuration must not stop the component from initializing.

- Catch `Throwable`, not just `ReflectiveOperationException` — it covers `LinkageError` and
  `NoClassDefFoundError` thrown by a custom class on an incomplete classpath.
- Log an error naming the config key and the real consequence, then fall back. Never throw
  out of a constructor.
- Word the message as what will happen ("Requests may be sent without a bearer token"), not
  merely the name of the fallback class.

Precedent: `RangerCustomConditionEvaluator`, `RangerGdsEnricher`, `JavaScriptEngineCreator`.

Related trap: do not construct a default object when the feature is unconfigured if some
`isXEnabled()` predicate keys off that object's presence — the feature then reports itself as
enabled for every caller. Return `null` and let callers null-check (RANGER-5795).

## 4. Running tests locally

`ranger-pr-review.mdc` covers `mvn -pl <module> -am -DskipTests verify`. To actually run tests:

```
mvn -q -pl agents-common test -Dtest='TestSomething' -DfailIfNoTests=false
```

- `-Dtest` takes a comma-separated list, not `+`.
- `-q` suppresses the pass counts. Read `<module>/target/surefire-reports/*.txt` instead.
- A local JaCoCo/JDK mismatch prints `Unsupported class file major version 70` instrumentation
  noise on stderr. It is unrelated to test results.
- Bare `mvn checkstyle:check` runs default sun_checks and reports tens of thousands of bogus
  violations. The project config is bound to `verify` via
  `configLocation=./dev-support/checkstyle.xml`.
